    https://github.com/wittawatj/jtcc/blob/master/TCC.g
  Python code: Korakot Chaovavanich
TCC rules proposed by Theeramunkong et al. 2000:
https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.59.2548

Modifications: finite allocation-free C++ predicates instead of Python regular
expressions; end-bounded UTF-8 decoding and streaming undecidability; a preceding
เ + base + ื + optional tone + อ + optional ะ correction; coalescing dependent
signs, retaining orphan signs with the following cluster, and bounded malformed
run fallback. Upstream alternative order, optional-group greediness, lookahead,
and the literal vertical bar in the upstream suffix character class are retained.
No Python runtime or general regular-expression engine is used on the device.
